# Git worktrees are created under `.claude/worktrees/<id>/`, i.e. INSIDE the
# repo, so each one is a second full copy of the tree. Without this exclusion
# Nx's project discovery walks into them and finds every project twice
# ("shared-errors: libs/shared/errors, .claude/worktrees/<id>/libs/shared/errors"),
# which fails every `nx` command run from the main checkout while a worktree
# exists. A worktree runs Nx from its own root, where this path does not apply,
# so it stays fully functional.
#
# `vitest.config.ts` excludes `**/.claude/**` for the same underlying reason —
# keep the two in step.
.claude/
